0007 — TP=2 multi-stream batched-verification gate (C=4 scaling audit)
========================================================================

Background / root cause
-----------------------
With 0006 (fused W8A16) live on the Qwen3.8-27B-8bit TP=2 pair
(spark1 .139 / spark2 .150, TensorFold v0.6.0), C=1 with DFlash2 measured
32.2 tok/s (prose) / 71.5 tok/s (code) while "C=4 x 512 with DFlash2"
measured only 24.5 tok/s aggregate — an apparent multi-stream inversion.

Phase 1 read-only audit (2026-10-23) found NO B>1 code defect:

1. The 24.5 tok/s figure was a harness artifact, not an engine defect.
   The original bench script compared the draft flag as d=="true" while
   invoking with D=on, so every "C=4 DFlash2" request went out as
   draft:false. 4 streams x 1 token / 163 ms (draft-off floor) = 24.5
   tok/s — matches the "inverted" measurement to the decimal. A second
   harness bug (aggregator reading stale draft-false JSON paths)
   reproduced the same number.

2. DFlash2 multi-stream bypass (hypothetical): ABSENT.
   multi.py:427-431 puts every stream's draft block into ONE drafter
   pass; multi.py:442-444 issues ONE multi_tree_forward per round with
   all streams' windows in a single W-row batch (forward.py:300-317).
   decode_tp.py is the C=1-only path; Multi (multi.py) handles B>1.

3. Drafter per-slot loops (hypothetical): ABSENT.
   dflash2.py:189/257 the fast path is REQUIRED under TP=2
   (fast and bits==4); dflash2.py:503-510 runs one batched _layer_fast
   per layer over the concatenated token tensor; dflash2.py:532-541
   exactly 2 all_gather_into_tensor per round, batch-wide.

4. GDN/attention per-slot collectives (hypothetical): ABSENT.
   forward.py:357 one deltanet.tree per GDN layer; forward.py:376 one
   tree_attention per attention layer; forward.py:432/441 one
   deltanet.replay "covers all layers and streams"; forward.py:483
   torch._foreach_copy_ KV commit. Zero dist.* calls in forward.py.

5. TP collective count (authoritative, distributed.py):
   split_layer (distributed.py:101-133): column-parallel linears
   (attn.q/k/v, gdn.qkv/z/b/a, mlp.gate/up) = no collective;
   row-parallel linears = 1 all_gather_into_tensor each
   (distributed.py:267-284, default op; all_reduce only under
   TF_TP_REDUCE=allreduce). Each of the 64 layers is EITHER GDN
   (gdn.out + mlp.down) OR attention (attn.o + mlp.down) = 2
   collectives -> total 128 per forward, COUNT B-INVARIANT (payload
   scales with rows). Live-confirmed: 128.0 stable across 800+ rounds.
   row_partial stored-layout cap: 128 rows (distributed.py:240).
   max_rows=16 (multi.py:86-90) is PER STREAM — C=4 full trees fit.

6. 0006 W8A16 kernel at M=32: FLAT.
   Micro-bench at the real per-rank shape (N=17408 K=2560 GS=64):
   M=1/4/8/32 = 0.244/0.246/0.248/0.264 ms/layer (+8% over 32x rows,
   memory-bound ~180 GB/s). The +44 ms/round M=8->32 in the engine cost
   curve is GDN tree compute + attention KV reads + NCCL payload, not
   the W8A16 matmul.

Live log audit: 0006 fast-path shape histogram (2,473,150 calls,
fallback: 0) shows M = total window rows across all streams in a single
GEMM (M=32/64 entries present at C=4; zero per-stream M=8 calls) —
the scheduler already batches exactly what this patch was scoped to add.

Measured result with drafts genuinely on (temp=0, enable_thinking=false,
512 tok/stream, same-session C=1 baseline):
  Prose: C=1 29.3  C=2 46.5 (1.59x)  C=4 75.5 (2.58x)
  Code:  C=1 60.8  C=2 97.4 (1.60x)  C=4 139.9-152 (2.30-2.50x)
  Greedy parity: C=4 streams byte-identical to C=1 (prose
  d5589b366369, code 39191bf72982); concurrent same-prompt streams
  identical to each other — no cross-stream KV/GDN state bleed.

Conclusion: the stock TP=2 scheduler already implements the batched
verification this patch's scope described. 0007 therefore ships as a
gate + invariant verification + harness fixes (user decision A): the
batched behavior becomes explicit, continuously checked, and
one-env-var revertible.

What ships
----------
1. /patches/tp2batchverify.py (new, top-level module, mirrors the
   0006 tp2w8a16.py pattern):
     TP2_BATCH_VERIFY=1 (default) - installs three lightweight hooks:
       - multi.MultiDecoder._verify        (round boundary)
       - multi.multi_tree_forward          (target-forward count)
       - distributed.gather_rank_partials  (collective count; patched on
         the distributed module because forward.py:30 and dflash2.py:481
         import it function-locally and re-resolve the attribute on
         every call)
     Bookkeeping only: two function calls per round. Optional stderr
     summary every 50 rounds via TP2_BATCH_VERIFY_DIAG=1:
       tp2batchverify: rounds=50 streams=200 rows=... fwd/round=1.00
                       target-colls/round=128.0 OK
     Invariants: exactly 1 multi_tree_forward per round and 128 target
     collectives per forward (2 per layer: {attn.o|gdn.out} + mlp.down). Drafter
     gathers (its own row-parallel linears + 2 candidate gathers) are
     counted in the total but not in the target invariant. A violated
     invariant logs one WARN line per rank.
     TP2_BATCH_VERIFY=0 - kill-switch: install() returns before any
     hook; pure stock path (mirrors TP2_W8A16=0 restoring the stock
     kernel).

2. /patches/tensorfold/__init__.py (+ staged tensorfold_init.py):
   appended 0007 install block after the 0006 block, same
   fail-soft pattern ("an optional patch must never break the server").

3. launch-tp2.sh: new env line (both nodes):
   -e TP2_BATCH_VERIFY="${TP2_BATCH_VERIFY:-1}" \
   -e TP2_BATCH_VERIFY_DIAG="${TP2_BATCH_VERIFY_DIAG:-1}" \
   (diag=1 in production, matching the TP2_W8A16_DIAG=1 precedent —
   continuous invariant evidence for the log-audit item.)

4. Harness v4 (bench/): w8a16_cn.sh / w8a16_c4.sh — label+concurrency
   keyed request/response paths (w8a16_<label>_c<N>_<i>.json), rm -f
   stale files first, draft flag set via argv comparison (draft:
   sys.argv[2]=='true') and echoed per request. Fixes both artifact
   bugs (flag compare, stale-JSON reuse) plus the _c4_ hardcoded
   response suffix.

Rollback
--------
TP2_BATCH_VERIFY=0 in launch-tp2.sh (or env) and one boot cycle:
0007 installs nothing, engine runs pure stock v0.6.0 + 0006. Or delete
patches/tp2batchverify.py and revert the two appended __init__ lines
(pre-patch copies: .bak-0007 in each node's patches/ dir). No image
state is modified at any point.

